---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you scope a project?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You describe the problem. I write a scope document listing the deliverables, integration points, testing criteria, and exclusions. Then I quote against that scope. Nothing ambiguous. You know what is being built before anything starts."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens if scope changes mid-build?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Scope changes get discussed before additional work begins. I do not surprise you at the end. If you want to add something or pivot, we talk about it, scope it, approve it, and then I build it. The original scope stays the original scope."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does a typical project take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most projects scope in one to two weeks and deliver in two to four. Bigger builds run longer. The scope document includes the timeline so there's no guessing. If something is going to slip, you hear about it before the deadline, not after."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens after delivery?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You get written handoff documentation covering configuration, credentials, and maintenance procedures. There's a short warranty window where I fix anything that breaks because of how it was built. After that, ongoing support is either a separate retainer or you handle it in-house. Your call."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you work with our existing systems or replace them?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Almost always I work with what you have. Most clients already have a CRM, an email tool, an analytics setup. They're just not connected to each other or configured correctly. Replacing a working system is usually the wrong move. I'll tell you when it isn't."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you fix things or only build new things?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Both. A lot of implementation work is fixing what's already there. Form submissions disappearing into a folder nobody checks. Analytics that's installed but not configured. Integrations that broke six months ago and nobody noticed. If it's a scoped project, I can take it on."
      }
    }
  ]
});

const serviceSchema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Implementation",
  "url": "https://codyasmith.com/services/implementation",
  "description": "CRM integrations, page builds, analytics setup, features, and scoped build work with a start and a finish.",
  "provider": { "@id": "https://codyasmith.com/#organization" },
  "serviceType": "Implementation and Build Work",
  "areaServed": { "@type": "Country", "name": "United States" },
  "termsOfService": "Scoped against a written scope document before execution. Production deployment includes handoff documentation."
});
---

<Base title="Implementation | Scoped Build Work" description="CRM integrations, page builds, analytics setup, features, and scoped build work with a start and a finish." ogImage="/og/services/implementation.png" ogImageAlt="Implementation: scoped build work. Start, build, hand over.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={serviceSchema} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://codyasmith.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Services","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Implementation","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services/implementation"}]})} />
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative pt-40 pb-24 px-6 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/3 w-[600px] h-[400px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-500 text-sm hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors duration-300 mb-8 group">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 16l-4-4m0 0l4-4m-4 4h18" />
        </svg>
        All services
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
        <span class="reveal text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em]">03</span>
        <div class="reveal gradient-divider flex-1"></div>
      </div>
      <h1 class="reveal font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl text-neutral-100 leading-[1.05] mb-6">
        Implementation
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-500 italic text-sm tracking-wide mb-10">Scoped projects. Start, build, hand over.</p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" data-frame="default">
        Someone fills out your contact form and the submission goes into a folder nobody checks. Your CRM doesn't know it happened. You find out three weeks later when you finally open that folder. These are the gaps between your website and your business. I build the connections that close them.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
        Your website and your business tools should talk to each other. Form submissions should land where your team works. Analytics should track actions you actually care about. New pages should fit the structure around them. I scope it, build it, and hand it over working.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
        Someone fills out your contact form and the submission goes into a folder nobody checks. Your CRM doesn't know it happened. These are the gaps between your website and your business. I build the connections that close them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Project types -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Project types</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">The kinds of things I build.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" data-vibe="default">
          Integrations, page builds, and analytics setup. Scoped projects with clear deliverables.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="beach">
          Your website, CRM, analytics, and pages should not feel like separate rooms. These are the scoped projects that connect the rooms.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          This is the engineering that makes everything reliable. Proper integrations, correct analytics, pages built on solid architecture. Every connection tested, documented, and handed over working.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8 reveal-stagger">
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-8" style="--i:0">
          <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
            <div class="lg:col-span-2">
              <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-4">Integrations</h3>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed mb-4" data-processing="default">
                Your forms submit but nothing happens on the other end. Leads don't reach your CRM. Email sequences never fire. Payment confirmations vanish. The connections between your site and your business tools are either broken or they never existed.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">
                I build those connections. Form submissions that land in your CRM tagged and ready. Email sequences that trigger when someone downloads a guide. Payment links that report clearly.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">
                Most integrations break in failure modes nobody tested: timeouts, malformed payloads, silent failures. The connections I build assume the failure modes happen, log them, and recover. Every integration ships with a runbook for what to check when something looks off.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">
                Form submissions land in your CRM. Email sequences fire when they should. Payment confirmations don't disappear. The connections work, and they keep working.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border-l border-white/5 pl-8">
              <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-4">Common projects</p>
              <ul class="text-neutral-300 text-sm space-y-3">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Gravity Forms → Pipedrive
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Brevo email automation
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  WooCommerce + payment
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Custom webhook flows
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal glow-card p-8" style="--i:1">
          <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
            <div class="lg:col-span-2">
              <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-4">Page builds</h3>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed mb-4" data-frame="default">
                The pages that need to exist for your marketing to make sense. You need location pages for three markets you're entering. Your homepage hasn't been rewritten since 2020 and it shows. Your pricing page reads like a legal document.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-frame="default">
                I handle everything from the keyword-targeted content architecture to the actual build in WordPress. You review, approve, and it goes live.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
                Pages built to compound over time. Location pages with the local search architecture each region needs, service pages structured for organic ranking on their own terms, homepage rewrites that close the gap between what the business does and what visitors think it does.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
                Pages that close the obvious gaps: underexplained pricing pages, homepages stuck two years behind your business, location pages that should exist but don't. The build covers the page strategy, structure, and WordPress implementation.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border-l border-white/5 pl-8">
              <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-4">Common projects</p>
              <ul class="text-neutral-300 text-sm space-y-3">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Location landing pages
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Service/product pages
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Homepage rewrites
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Pricing pages
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal glow-card p-8" style="--i:2">
          <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
            <div class="lg:col-span-2">
              <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-4">Analytics setup</h3>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed mb-4" data-processing="default">
                Most sites have analytics installed. Very few have analytics configured clearly. Your GA4 might be running, but if events, filters, and reports are not set up around the questions you ask, the data is just noise pretending to be signal.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">
                I configure GA4, Google Search Console, Microsoft Clarity, and event tracking so the numbers you see actually mean something.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">
                The configuration question isn't "is it installed" but "is it tuned." Events fire on actions that match a buyer decision. Conversions trigger only when the action completes. Every dashboard cleans up because every input is intentional.
              </p>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">
                Analytics that answer the question instead of producing noise. Configured once, kept clean, so the next decision you make can come from data instead of vibes.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border-l border-white/5 pl-8">
              <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-4">Common projects</p>
              <ul class="text-neutral-300 text-sm space-y-3">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  GA4 configuration
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Search Console setup
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Conversion tracking
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="text-amber-400 mt-1.5 text-[8px]">&#9670;</span>
                  Cookie consent compliance
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How projects work -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 dot-grid">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Process</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">How projects work.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 reveal-stagger">
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6 text-center" style="--i:0">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-amber-400 text-sm font-mono font-bold">1</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Scope</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">You describe the problem. I define exactly what's included, what's not, and what it takes to ship.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">You tell me what outcome you need. I define what it takes to get there.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Written scope document listing every deliverable, integration point, testing criteria, and exclusion. Nothing ambiguous.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6 text-center" style="--i:1">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/70 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-amber-400/70 text-sm font-mono font-bold">2</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Quote</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Written quote. Clear scope. No "we'll figure it out later" bucket.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">One agreed shape before work starts. No surprises on either side.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Quote based on the scope document. Scope changes discussed before additional work begins.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6 text-center" style="--i:2">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/50 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-amber-400/50 text-sm font-mono font-bold">3</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Build</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">I build it. You get updates. If scope changes, we discuss it before the work changes.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">I build it and keep you in the loop. You focus on your business.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Development with progress updates at each milestone. Staging environment for review. Scope changes documented and quoted before execution.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6 text-center" style="--i:3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/30 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-amber-400/30 text-sm font-mono font-bold">4</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Deliver</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">You review, I revise if needed, it goes live. Documentation included so your team knows what changed.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">You review, approve, and it's live. Your team gets documentation so they can own it going forward.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Client review, revision round, production deployment, and written handoff documentation covering configuration, credentials, and maintenance procedures.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Mid-page CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center reveal">
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-4">Have something that needs building?</p>
      <a href="/contact?interest=implementation" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 border border-white/10 text-neutral-300 font-medium text-sm rounded-lg hover:border-amber-500/25 hover:text-amber-400 transition-all duration-300">
        Tell me what you need
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Scope note -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Scope</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-8">Scoped before built.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Implementation starts with scope. Once I understand what needs to be built, I give you a written quote, timeline, handoff shape, and exclusions before work begins.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm">
          If the request is really Strategy Consulting, Web Management, or Training, I will say that before turning it into a build.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Questions</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">Things people ask.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 reveal-stagger">
        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:0">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            How do you scope a project?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            You describe the problem. I write a scope document listing the deliverables, integration points, testing criteria, and exclusions. Then I quote against that scope. Nothing ambiguous. You know what is being built before anything starts.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:1">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What happens if scope changes mid-build?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Scope changes get discussed before additional work begins. I do not surprise you at the end. If you want to add something or pivot, we talk about it, scope it, approve it, and then I build it. The original scope stays the original scope.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:2">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            How long does a typical project take?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Most projects scope in one to two weeks and deliver in two to four. Bigger builds run longer. The scope document includes the timeline so there's no guessing. If something is going to slip, you hear about it before the deadline, not after.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:3">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What happens after delivery?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            You get written handoff documentation covering configuration, credentials, and maintenance procedures. There's a short warranty window where I fix anything that breaks because of how it was built. After that, ongoing support is either a separate retainer or you handle it in-house. Your call.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:4">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            Do you work with our existing systems or replace them?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Almost always I work with what you have. Most clients already have a CRM, an email tool, an analytics setup. They're just not connected to each other or configured correctly. Replacing a working system is usually the wrong move. I'll tell you when it isn't.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:5">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            Do you fix things or only build new things?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Both. A lot of implementation work is fixing what's already there. Form submissions disappearing into a folder nobody checks. Analytics that's installed but not configured. Integrations that broke six months ago and nobody noticed. If it's a scoped project, I can take it on.
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="relative py-32 px-6 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[500px] h-[300px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
